        <p>PUBLIC MEN SPEAK HIGHLY Or IT ALL OVER TM WORLD. Dowlais, Merthyr Tydfil, Glamorgan, July, 1892. DEAR SIR,—I must write to say that your Tudor Williams' Balsam of Honey for Coughs is the best we ever had in the house. My biv David had a cough which shook him from top to toe, couldn' sleep at night for it, ani neither could anyone else in the house el ep hecause of his harking. A few doses of Balsa nof Honey positively cured him ; it is a wonderful cure.</p>
        <p>DAVID JONES. Escz., High Constable.</p>
