      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-10-20_WidnesExaminer_art0064" n="art0064">
        <head>FRODSHAM.</head>
        <p>FRODSHAM.</p>
        <p>HE FELL INTO RAD CoMPANY.—AnniP Lane,ll, Parry's- entry ; Wm. Mi!Dermott and Peter O'Brien (of no fixed residence) were charged on remand at the Chester Police Court, on Friday, before Mr. R. Frost and Dr. St.lterfoth, the woman with stealing about £lB, the money ot Henry Hinde, Frodsham. and the two men with receiving part of the moner knowing it to have ty en stolen. The case against O'Brien was dismissed, McDermott, who pleaded " guilty," was sent to gaol for four months ; and Lane, who pleaded "not guilty," was sent to the Sessions. Smbsequently O'Brien was sent to gaol for a month for assaulting a man named Higgins, by hitting him on the head with a jam jar.</p>
        <p>,</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-10-20_WidnesExaminer_art0065" n="art0065">
