      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-10-20_WidnesExaminer_art0066" n="art0066">
        <head>SHOOTING MATCH BETWEEN RUNCORN AND WIDNES VOLUNTEERS.</head>
        <p>SHOOTING MATCH BETWEEN RUNCORN AND WIDNES VOLUNTEERS.</p>
        <p>An interesting shooting match between a team of ten men belonging to the Widnes Company of the 2nd (Prince of Wales' Own) Volunteer Batts- lion, South Lancashire Regiment, and a like num- ber from the Runcorn Shooting Club, attached to the 2nd kEarl of Chester's) Volunteer RAttalion Cheshire Regiment took place on Saturd,ty afternoon on the Wid- nes range. The contest began soon after 1.30 under Risley regulations as to targets and position. The follow- ing scores will show that the Runcornians ended victor- iously by 34 points : Rank and Names</p>
        <p>nusconN TEAM. 500 200 To-</p>
        <p>yds. yds. tal. Sergt. W. H. Harvey Private J. Houghton Private J. P. Edwards 3O ... 26 ... 56 Band-Sergeant J. Gittens 25 ... 31 ... 56 Sergeant J. A. Rushton Sergeant W. Nield Serjeant G. R. Joynson Sergeant W. Cooper 26 ... 23 ... 54 Colour-Sergeant J. Poole Colour-sergeant J. Mort.</p>
        <p>Totals 281 264 545 WIDNES TEA 31.</p>
        <p>500 200 To-</p>
        <p>yds. yds. tel. Sergeant W. Dwerryhouse 3O ... 33 ... 63 Sergeant G. Junor Private R. Campbell Corporal L. Roberts Corporal J. Foster Private j. Swirt 24 ... 24 ... 48 Private D. Griffiths 2l ... 26 ... 47 Private J. Taylor Private J. G. Robinson Colour Sergeant W. H. Davies lB ... 24 ... 42</p>
        <p>Totals</p>
        <p>After the match the competitors named, accom- panied by other members of the respective corps ad- journed to the Widnes Drill Hall, and partook of a hot supper. The evening was spent in a convivial manner.</p>
