      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-10-20_WidnesExaminer_art0069" n="art0069">
        <head>A. TIMELY WARNING.</head>
        <p>A. TIMELY WARNING.</p>
        <p>Never trust those who promise too much at a time The patent medicines which pretend to cure " at once," in "a single dose," or in "ten minutes," convince us that they are Unnatural in their operation, and that, therefore, either the promise made is a false one, or that the remedy is worse than the disease. It is not "at once" that a man becomes Consumptive ; it is not " at a single meal" that you acquire Indigestion and Dyspepsia ; it is not in" ten minutes " that your Liver becomes slugrrish and out of order. No. These com- plaints and others which might be named are gradual in their hold to release you " at once," "in ten minutes" or" at a single dose." .?.s the disease, so its cure. Steady and certain is its approach. Steady and certain should be its retreat. It is in this fact that the secret of the wonderful, the unparalleled success of Gwilym Evans Quinine Bitters lies. It conforms to Nature's Jaws, adapts itsvlf to Nature's requirements. If the constitution has been slowly, steadiy, and certainly undermined by disease, so it is slowly, steadily, anil certainly re-built by this excellent rermedr. It does not pretend to miraculous instantaneous effect cures. If the disease is deep-rooted and of long standing, a sudden and forcible uprooting would do more harm than good. Gwilym Evans' Quinin• Bitters loosen first one hold of the disease on the body, then another and yet another, taking away one by onl the clammy fingers of disease and replacing them with the warm glowing touch of health and new life, not only removing the di-,ease effectually, but giving New Life with every dose taken. The more recent the disease the more easily removed. • Overwork ought to be overpaid. Nature insists upon payment of her first dues. Intense devotion to busi- ness gives the digestive organs only a bare chance to perform their work. He who comes in a hurry from active work, rapidly swallows his food and hurries out again, is piling up a debt which nature makes him pay in a painful dyspeps4ic experience. Gwilvm Evans's Quinine Bitters will help you to pay, and the sooner you take it the better.</p>
        <p>-- Try this r;reat Natural remedy. Try it :now. Recovered Patients say it is an Unfailinz Remedy. Everybody says it is the Best Remedy of the Age.</p>
        <p>TUE VEGETABLE TONIC.</p>
        <p>GWILYM EVANS'S QUININE BITTERS.</p>
        <p>Sold in Bottles at 1/IA, 2/9, and 4/6 each. Beware of Imitations See the name of " G WILYM Eves" on Label Stamp and Bottle. SOLE PROPRIETORS: QUININE BITTERS MANUFACTURING CO., LTD., LLANELLY, SOUTH WALES.</p>
