      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1894-10-20_WidnesExaminer_art0085" n="art0085">
        <p>!JOHN WALKER AND C PROPRIETORS OF THE EXAMINER SERIES OF</p>
        <p>LANCASHIRE &amp; CHESHIRE COUNTY NEWSPAPERS</p>
        <p>WHICH COMPRISE rTHE Warrington 4- Mid-Cheshire Examiner, pub- lished Saturday morning. The district covered by the Paper comprises many populous manufacturing -towns and villages, and a large agricultural tract. THE Earlestown and Newton Examiner, and Ashton, Colborne, and Haydock Reporter, published FridaY afternoon. The district is in the heart of the Lancashire coal field.</p>
        <p>rr HE St. Helens Examtner and Prescot Weekly News, pn blished Friday afternoon. The district comprises the centre of the Glass, Chemical, and Watch Trades of the King' OM. &amp;C.</p>
        <p>THE Runcorn Examiner, published Friday after- -1 noon. It is the only Weekly Paper in the•district. and offers the best and cheapest facilities to advertisers.</p>
        <p>T HE Widn,ls Examiner, published Friday after- noon. Widnes contains the largest number of Chenai.cal Works of any town in the kingdom, and is rapidly becoming an important centre of industry.</p>
        <p>Auction, Education, Wanted, To he Let, On Sale, Leff?! Public Meeting, Sermon, Lecture, Bazaar, and other PubliC Notices, Advertisements (except Parliamentary)are inserted 113 all the above papers at one charge.</p>
        <p>Each of the above papers consists of 8 pages. 56 long and wide columns,each column admitting more matter than the eolumns of any otherloca.l paper—a fact deserving the atisa lion of both advertisers and subscribers. Each Exammer, 115 4ddition to giving the local intelligence of the district. in which it circulates, contains the general news of the week.</p>
        <p>Price of each Paper—ONE PENNY.</p>
