        <p>AN ENGLISHMAN'S HOUSE IS HIS CASTLE or, properly speaking, ought to be. This Cart never be the case, if .unfortunately a would-be householder has to resort to the Easy Payment System, a new name for the ini- quitous Hire System. To furnish a house on the Hire System. alias the Easy Payment System, is to establish and support what is the most cruel, arbitrary extortion ever invented. The prices charged for the goods are enormous, without any regard for quality, the agreements are one-sided, being drawn with a cuteness which would do credit to a money lender, full of despotic and arbitrary restrictions, such as not to remove the mark on the furniture, not to remove the furniture, not to wear the furniture. At all times to allow the mercenaries to inspect the furniture. To ply the instal- ments regularly, and if oneis missed to forfeit the furniture and all the moneys you may have paid, that is to say, although you might have paid £l9 on £2) worth of furniture, but missed the last payment by a single day, the vultures could empty your house and stick to the £l9 paid, as well as the furniture. Other conditions such as permission to break open forcibly night or day, the outer and inner doors of your house, in order to take away the goods, and above all, that no matter how badly and wickedly they may treat you that you undertake not to resort to legal proceedings. Be warned in time, have nothing to do with easy payment or hire system. If you require assistance go to Mr. W. H. Worsley, "The Pantheon," Gaythorne. Manchester, the largest House Fur- nisher in the North, who will treat you with consideration, sell you goods at the lowest cash price, and, if required, allow you time to pay for them, charging you 10 per cent over invoice price for the convenience. For instance Mr. Worsley has several HOUSES OF FUR- NITURE on view at £l5 155., £2O, £25, £3O. £59, £lOO, all at the lowest cash price, and not a penny less. Any of the above supplied subject to credit, upon