        <p>WARRINGTON OCCASIONAL COURT. At the above court on Tuesday, before the Mayor (Alderman Greens.ll), Joseph Bowers, alias Bate, was charged with having stolen a number of work- men's tools from the wheelwrights' shop at Waders- pool Brewery, the property of Thos. Woodward, John Sankey, and Josoph Moss, between 30th and 31st May, 1893. The prisoner was apprehended that morning on leaving Walton Gaol. In answer to the charge, prisoner said he knew nothing about the tools. He was committed to the next Cheshire Quarter Sessions.</p>
